\par\par \b \uc2 BASE METALS HIGHLIGHTS: Top Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2011\par 22:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  TOP STORIES: \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kazakhmys\f28 \uc2 \f2  Signs $1.5B Facility To Develop Aktogay Project \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON -(Dow Jones)- International natural resources group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kazakhmys PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KAZ.LN) said Friday it has now signed the $1.5 billion loan facility with \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  agreed in June to develop its Aktogay copper project in Kazakhstan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LME Says It Expects Bids For Exchange By End Of February \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The bidding process to buy the London Metal Exchange is under way, with the exchange in the process of sending nondisclosure agreements to third parties interested in submitting bids and information set to follow next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  STORIES OF INTEREST: \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Peso Closes Firmer As \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Ends, Copper Rises \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso closed stronger against the dollar Friday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program came to its scheduled end and as international copper prices rose.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Polish Official: KGHM Can Pay PLN3B Dividend Or More - Report \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 KGHM Polska Miedz SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KGH.WA), Europe's second-largest copper miner controlled by the Polish government, has the ability to pay an annual dividend at 3 billion zlotys ($869 million) or more, Poland's Treasury Minister Mikolaj Budzanowski is quoted as saying by state newswire PAP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Poland's KGHM To Assess Impact Of Proposed Mining Tax Before Commenting \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Polish copper producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 KGHM Polska Miedz SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KGH.WA) will need to conduct an assessment of the impact of the government's proposed mining tax on the company before commenting on it, KGHM spokesman Dariusz Wyborski said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oz Minerals\f28 \uc2 \f2  Annual Copper Resource Estimate Rises, Gold Falls \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MELBOURNE (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Oz Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (OZL.AU) said Friday it has increased the copper resource estimate for its sole mine in Australia, although it trimmed the gold resource estimate and said overall reserves have been depleted by mining.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Most 1Q Japan Aluminum Premiums Settle At $112/Ton -Sources \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Most Japanese aluminum premiums for first-quarter shipments have settled at $112 a metric ton, down from this quarter's level of $118-$119/ton, amid slack domestic demand, trader and consumer sources told Dow Jones Newswires Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  MARKETS: \par  \par BASE METALS: Copper Bounces 2%, Snaps Four-Day Losing Streak \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Copper prices locked in their first gain in five days Friday as some investors closed out bets on lower prices ahead of the holiday season while others treated a weaker dollar and recent declines as a bargain-hunting opportunity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tatyana Shumsky, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3095; tatyana.shumsky@dowjones.com [ 12-16-11 1623ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 61063 82202   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111216e7cg0007o\par }\p