\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Closes Firmer As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Ends, Copper Rises\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2011\par 18:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed stronger against the dollar Friday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program came to its scheduled end and as international copper prices rose.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP517.50 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP518.20. It traded in a range of CLP516.10 to CLP519.10.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile is the world's premier copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, traders and investors keep track of New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 The most active contract for copper futures, for March delivery, was recently up 5.65 cents, or 1.7%, at $3.3235 a pound on the Comex division of the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , as some progress was seen on confronting the euro zone's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 In addition, rising U.S. markets, as investors digested improving domestic economic data, helped to boost the peso. U.S. markets are often seen as a bellwether for risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 "In general, today has been a good day for markets, especially considering copper prices rising well above 1%. That's lifting the peso," said Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on the last day of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP517.59 to the dollar. It accumulated $12.0 billion during the year through the program.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicked off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, which sought to increase the bank's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to the equivalent of 17% of gross domestic product, in early January when the peso was trading near a three-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 As exports represent roughly 60% of the country's gross domestic product, a stronger peso cuts into these products' competitiveness abroad.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program had the immediate effect of punching the air out of the peso's strength, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gradually climbed back and was trading at three-year highs in July as nervous participants worried about U.S. debt and growth.\par \par \uc2 Then, as concerns about Europe's sovereign-debt crisis congealed in investors' psyche and international copper prices dropped, the peso weakened to 16-month lows in early October.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in a light trading session.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged at 2.41%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.53%, from 2.52% the prior session. Bond prices and yields move in opposite directions.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 16-12-11 1710GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111216e7cg000w