\par\par \b \uc2 Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Extends $50M Daily Purchases Through Dec 8\b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 20:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ("Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Extends $50M Daily Purchases Through Dec 8," at 14:49 EST, misstated the end date for the new phase of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchasing program in the headline, first and second paragraphs. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will continue with the current pace of its peso market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program through Dec. 7, the bank said on its website Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 It will continue buying $50 million a day from Nov. 9 through Dec. 7 as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for 2011.\par \par \uc2 In early January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to beat back the peso as it was trading at three-year highs versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent, a strong peso hurts exporters' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Although the peso weakened substantially and slid to a 16-month low in early October, as worries about Europe's sovereign debt crisis battered international copper prices, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed the course of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. In recent weeks, the peso has recovered some ground as progress is seen in tackling Europe's debt troubles.\par \par \uc2 Through the purchases, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to the equivalent of 17% of gross domestic product by year-end.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $10.65 billion as a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to data the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported on Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves at the end of October totaled $38.67 billion compared with $37.84 billion in reserves at the end of September.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 08-11-11 2042GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111108e7b8001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
