\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Extends $50M Daily Purchases Through Nov 8\b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 21:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 7 Oct 2011 15:45 EDT DJ  Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Extends $50M Daily Purchases Through Nov 8\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't alter the pace of its peso-market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program and will continue its daily dollar purchases through Nov. 8, the bank said on its website Friday.\par \par \uc2 With the peso weakening around 12% in September, many market participants were speculating that the bank would wrap up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the scheduled December end date.\par \par \uc2 The bank will continue buying $50 million a day from Oct. 11 through Nov. 8 as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan for 2011.\par \par \uc2 In early January, when the peso was trading at three-year highs against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicked off its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of Friday, the bank had bought $9.7 billion so far this year in its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With the dollar purchases, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to the equivalent of 17% of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 According to data the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported early Friday, Chile's foreign reserves at the end of September rose to $37.84 billion, from $36.37 billion at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 07, 2011 15:45 ET (19:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111007e7a7005tz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
