\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECT (9/29): Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief Doesn't Rule Out Rate Cut\b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 22:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ("UPDATE: Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Doesn't Rule Out Rate Cut," at 1533 GMT Thursday, misstated the September direction of the peso in the thirteenth paragraph. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not ruling out interest rate cuts in coming months\par \par \uc2 --Local markets already factoring in rate cut by January\par \par \uc2 --Bank constantly evaluating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday he isn't ruling out an interest rate reduction, in light of growing international risks, especially in Europe.\par \par \uc2 In its quarterly Monetary Policy Report released earlier this month, the bank based its baseline scenario on the benchmark rate holding steady through December.\par \par \uc2 "We aren't married to this baseline scenario," bank head Jose De Gregorio said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has held the benchmark overnight lending rate steady at 5.25% for three consecutive months after a series of increases.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bi-weekly poll of traders' expectations showed these market participants see the benchmark rate retreating to 5% by January 2012 and to 4.75% by April of next year.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio, speaking at a seminar hosted by the Chilean-American Chamber of Commerce, or Amcham, said the economic outlook in Europe poses the greatest international risk.\par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Europe's woes are occurring in "slow motion, like an accident in a tunnel where everyone is driving without headlights," but noted that there won't likely be a crash like there was in 2008 with \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 ' troubles.\par \par \uc2 He added that the bank has the policies to act should economic conditions abroad worsen.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the recent depreciation the peso has posted against the dollar, De Gregorio said the drop was in line with weakening seen in other commodity-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world.\par \par \uc2 "With commodities prices falling, we have to expect some sort of peso depreciation," he said.\par \par \uc2 As Chile produces a third of the world's copper, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes cues from international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 In early 2011, when the peso was trading at three-year highs against the dollar, on strong growth expectations and rising copper prices, the bank announced a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 In light of the near 12% drop the peso has seen so far in September, analysts have been speculating the bank could end its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program early.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said the bank is always evaluating its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "But that's the same response I would have had if asked about the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  three months ago," he told conference participants.\par \par \uc2 He noted that incentives for carry-trade \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Chilean peso had decreased recently on the retreat in the longer-term rate outlook.\par \par \uc2 The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to end in December.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; +56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 09-30-11 1619ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110930e79u000y6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
