\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real gains after  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  swap; Latam rebounds\b0\par\par\uc2 846 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 18:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil c. bank swap sale checks real slide, sets 'limit'\par \par \uc2 * Mexico, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  pesos rebound from sharp Thursday declines\par \par \uc2 * Peru \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market; sol erases loss\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds Brazil, Peru, Colombia comment)\par \par \uc2 By Jeb Blount\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Brazil's real reversed losses to gain more than 3 percent against the dollar on Friday -- its biggest one-day gain in almost 16 months -- after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day earlier raised expectations it will act again to limit sharp falls.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's sale of $2.75 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps effectively put a limit on how far the bank will allow the real to slide, said Mario Battistel, head of trading at Fair Corretora, a Sao Paulo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage. For more see [ID:nS1E78L0PK].\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps mimic the sale of dollars and provide investors with insurance against future declines in the real.\par \par \uc2 The real has lost more than 15 percent of its value since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly cut its benchmark interest rate by half a percentage point to 12 percent on Aug. 31. The move was based on the bank's expectation that a world economic slowdown would push down Brazil's 7 percent inflation rate. [ID:nE5E7IM05G] and [ID:nL3E7KN1BZ]\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a pleasant surprise," Battistel said in a telephone interview. "They're clearly worried about inflation and exporters and our other clients weren't about to start moving their large dollar holdings back into Brazil until they had some idea of when the real's plunge would stop."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> gained 3.19 percent to 1.8360 to the U.S. dollar, its first gain in six sessions and its biggest one-day gain since May 27, 2010.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lost more than 1 percent in early trade and still ended the week down about 5.75 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The government is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb wide swings, or volatility, in the market, Finance Minster Guido Mantega told investors in Washington. [ID:nS1E78M134]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets inflation of 4.5 percent plus or minus 2 percentage points and has long said that inflation, now outside the target range, will come under control soon.\par \par \uc2 A strong real helps control inflation by cutting the cost of dollar-denominated commodities such as food and the cost of essential imports such as machine-tools for Brazil's industry.\par \par \uc2 Battistel said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which as recently as August was working to prevent the real from gaining against the dollar, is signaling that it will act any time the real weakens beyond 1.90 to the dollar or strengthens beyond 1.60.\par \par \uc2 Other traders said the bank is targeting the first dollar futures contract <DOLc1> on the Sao Paulo BM&FBovespa exchange, moving to weaken the real when it firms beyond 2.01 to the dollar and to strengthen the real when it weakens beyond 1.78.\par \par \uc2 The real-dollar spot exchange rate's close link to the futures market, where bets can be ramped up using loans or "leverage" is one of the reasons the real lost so much in recent weeks, the government said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In first futures trading, which measure expectations for late September, the real shed 2.16 percent to 1.8585.\par \par \uc2 Bets on a strong real were a key component in the real's nearly 8 percent rise through late July.\par \par \uc2 Since then the real has reversed all those gains and is now about 9 percent weaker than it was at the end of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Latin America \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded from steep Thursday declines on expectation losses related to concern about a potential Greek default may be overdone.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=D2> jumped 3.63 percent to 13.5584 to the dollar, reversing some of Thursday's losses that took the peso beyond 14 to the dollar for the first time since April 2009. For the week the peso trimmed losses to 3.89 percent.\par \par \uc2 "I think the market has pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too far too fast and we may see a bit of retracement in the peso's favor," said Francisco Diez, director of emerging-market trading at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The next point the peso will test if it begins weakening again is 14.25 to the dollar Diez said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> gained 0.93 percent to 516.00 to the dollar after plunging more than 5 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso <COP2=STFX> gained 0.58 percent to 1,904.\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol <PEN=PE> trimmed early losses to trade little changed from Thursday at 2.7700 after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $21 million dollars for pesos, driving up demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and helping it firm.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rachel Uranga in Mexico City; Editing by Raymond Colitt and Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n00198\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
