\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank eyes halting peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to evaluate calling an early end to a dollar purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program after a sharp depreciation of the local peso, bank President Jose De Gregorio told Diario Financiero's Friday edition.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio also told the newspaper that Chile has plenty of room to lower its key interest rate <CLINTR=ECI> after an aggressive cycle of hikes.\par \par \uc2 Battered by nosediving prices for Chile's main export, copper, and global bourses that have swooned on fears the United States and Europe could slip back into recession, Chile's peso <CLP=CL> fell 3.9 percent on Thursday to close at bid 520.80 per dollar, its weakest level since July 2010.\par \par \uc2 The bank's $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for 2012, introduced in January to tame a strong peso, is about two-thirds complete and is due to run until December.\par \par \uc2 "As we have said since the beginning, we will continue to evaluate (it) and see what the market is saying," De Gregorio told the newspaper during a visit to Washington for the International Monetary Fund and World Bank meetings.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said the bank, which held its key rate at 5.25 percent for a third month running in September as the economy slows amid global gloom, has room to cut. For details, see [ID:nS1E78E1T2]\par \par \uc2 "Chile has lots of space to cut its interest rate," De Gregorio told the paper. "Whether or not we cut will depend on macroeconomic conditions."\par \par \uc2 The bank, which has called an early halt to a rate-tightening cycle as the domestic economy and inflation moderate, is seen holding its key rate in the near term, but then cutting rates next year.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Simon Gardner; editing by Jeffrey Benkoe)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n000q8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
