\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher, Boosted By LAN, Track US Market Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2011\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Friday, as flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) surged after Brazilian authorities recommended approval of its proposed merger with Brazil's TAM (TAM, TAMM4.BR) and as the local market tracked rising U.S. shares.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa climbed 0.8% to 4248.35 points, paring back some of its earlier gains. Market volume, meanwhile, slipped to 94.42 billion Chilean pesos ($200.7 million), compared with CLP106.86 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As Monday is a religious holiday, all Chilean markets, banks and government offices will be closed.\par \par \uc2 After market close Thursday, Brazil's SEAE government antitrust regulation agency recommended the approval of LAN's planned merger with TAM.\par \par \uc2 The merger, which looks to create Latin America's largest airline and one of the 10 biggest airlines in the world, is awaiting a key ruling from Chile's TDLC antitrust court. That ruling is expected during August. Additionally, Brazil's CADE antitrust court must also approve the deal.\par \par \uc2 LAN's shares jumped 2.8% to CLP11,710.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, as several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the DJIA. The DJIA gained 125.71 points, or 1.1%, to 11269.02 as an upbeat retail sales report trumped a weak reading on consumer confidence.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, chemical and specialty-fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more-liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) increased 2.5% to CLP28,600.00 and bank \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  (BCA, CORPBANCA.SN) expanded 2.1% to CLP6.90.\par \par \uc2 For its part, energy holding company CGE (CGE.SN) leapt 7.9% to CLP2,550.00 after shareholders put an end to a shareholders agreement.\par \par \uc2 "The biggest shareholders, now that the shareholders agreement has been terminated, will fight for control of the company and that's going to boost share prices," said Desiree Soulodre, trader at brokerage BCI Corredor de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso closed slightly stronger versus the dollar, although it pared back most of its earlier gains, as participants closed positions before the long holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP470.50 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP470.90. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP467.70 to CLP471.80.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its continuing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP470.29 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.80 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower on decreasing private-sector inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 Private sector inflation expectations are retreating and moving toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation target of 3%, plus or minus one percentage point.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, from 2.65% Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.63%, from 2.66% the previous session\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 12-08-11 2034GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Doku