\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close 3.0% Higher, Tracking Surging US Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 3.0% higher Thursday, the local market's second biggest jump this year, as it tracked surging U.S. markets and continued recovering from recent steep losses.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa climbed to 4228.93 points, while market volume jumped to 106.86 billion Chilean pesos ($226.9 million), compared with Wednesday's closing volume of CLP98.77 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the DJIA. The Dow closed up 423 points Thursday after investors digested favorable corporate and economic data.\par \par \uc2 "The local market rose in line with global equity markets and as investors bought shares at attractive prices following several days of steep losses," said Gustavo Fingeret, analyst with investment bank Celfin Capital.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) gained 2.6% to CLP11,400.00 after the company's chief executive officer said he was optimistic LAN's proposed merger with Brazil's TAM would be approved soon. Chile's TDLC antitrust court is reviewing the merger and is expected to rule on it during August.\par \par \uc2 Also gaining, power generator \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) jumped 3.6% to CLP774.90; its parent company, energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN), climbed 3.3% to CLP186.50; and wine producer and exporter \uc2 Vina Concha y Toro\uc2  (VCO, CONCHATOR.SN) leapt 6.4% to CLP1,060.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, commodities-related companies surged after pulp-and-wood-products company CMPC's (CMPC.SN) strong second-quarter earnings, highlighting robust demand for their products and giving investors reasons to believe other commodities-related companies will also post firm quarterly earnings.\par \par \uc2 "If you look closely at Chilean companies, it's clear that they are \b \highlight22\uc2 operationally\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financially well positioned to continue growing at a fast pace," said Fingeret.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, chemical and specialty-fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more-liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) increased 4.1% to CLP27,850.00; integrated steel and iron-ore producer Cap (CAP.SN) rose 4.7% to CLP19,700.00; fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN) increased 0.8% to CLP7,700.00; and CMPC jumped 1.6% to CLP21,750.00.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso closed stronger versus the dollar, ending a five-day losing streak, as international copper prices jumped toward the $9,000-a-metric-ton mark following the better-than-expected U.S. jobs data.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP470.90 to the dollar, reversing its earlier losses, versus Wednesday's close of CLP473.20. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP470.30 to CLP477.40.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Thursday at an average rate of CLP475.20 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.75 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher as U.S. and local equity markets surged.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.65%, from 2.61% Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.66%, from 2.62% the previous session.\par 