\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 2.2% Higher On Retail Despite Drop In US Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2011\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 2.2% higher Wednesday, even as markets in the U.S. and Europe dropped sharply, as the retail sector and information technology firm Sonda (SONDA.SN) surged.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa climbed to 4094.09 points, while market volume slipped to 98.77 billion Chilean pesos ($208.7 million), compared with CLP159.81 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 Even though the DJIA recently dropped 538 points, as participants digested the Federal Reserve's downbeat assessment of the U.S. economy, the Ipsa rose as investors bought into the heavily punished Chilean retail sector.\par \par \uc2 Retailers fell broadly in recent weeks, first amid investigations into alleged fraud committed by department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN), and then on the back of intensifying double-dip recession fears.\par \par \uc2 "At these prices, retailers are very attractive and mutual funds snapped up sector shares," said Maria Jesus Bofill, trader at brokerage BCI Corredor de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) jumped 3.3% to CLP2,870.00 and department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) increased 2.4% to CLP4,120.00. Retailer Hites (HITES.SN) gained 7.0% to CLP413.00 and La Polar rose 0.9% to CLP454.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, Sonda surged 8.3% to CLP1,170.00 as investors applauded its plans to take over rival Quintec for $68.6 million and beef up its presence in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia and Peru.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN), the Ipsa's heaviest-weighted share, leapt 5.5% to CLP7,649.00 after its Arauco pulp and paper subsidiary said it would increase capacity to 3.3 million metric tons from 3.2 million tons.\par \par \uc2 With continuing fears about a double-dip recession in the U.S., concerns about Europe's unresolved sovereign debt woes, including worries France may be the next triple-A-rated country to face a credit downgrade, "investors should be cautious to jump back into equities markets," said Bofill.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso closed marginally weaker versus the dollar Wednesday, at a fresh eight-week low, as the euro fell sharply against the greenback on concerns France may be downgraded.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP473.20 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP473.00, while trading in a range of CLP469.90 to CLP474.70.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Wednesday at an average rate of CLP472.46 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.70 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower as fixed-income participants kept their eyes on the tricky scenario abroad and as local private pension fund managers bought bonds in a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheduled auction.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.61%, from 2.64% Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.62%, from 2.70% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 10-08-11 2024GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110810e78a001rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
