\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends At 8-Week Low As Copper Prices Continue Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2011\par 19:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended slightly weaker against the dollar Tuesday, at an eight-week low, as international copper prices continued to slide.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP473.00 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP472.30, while trading in a range of CLP472.60 to CLP475.30.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Three-month copper on the London Metal Exchange closed 0.6% lower at $8,731 per metric ton, weighed down by technical selling after its recent slump below $9,000 a ton.\par \par \uc2 The peso posted a 1.6% decline the prior session as the downgrade of U.S. debt saw institutional investors buying the safe-haven dollar.\par \par \uc2 "With copper's sharp decline in recent days, pressure mounted for the peso to fall," said Cristobal Aviles, trader at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, a mild reading of local consumer prices, reported the prior session, also helped to push the peso lower.\par \par \uc2 Chile's CPI posted a 0.1% gain in July, in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 "With the mild CPI reading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely not raise interest rates this month or maybe even next month either," said Aviles.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Tuesday at an average rate of CLP474.90 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher as equities markets around the globe rebounded from Monday's rout.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.64%, from 2.60% Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.70%, from 2.64% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 09-08-11 1750GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110809e789001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
