\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Suffer Biggest One-Day Slump In Nearly 13 Years\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2011\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 6.9% lower Monday, suffering its biggest one-day slump since the Asian financial crisis of 1998 and technically entering bear-market territory.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa dropped below the 4000-point mark for the first time since June 2008, amid a global rout in equities markets as \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  unprecedented decision to downgrade U.S. debt late Friday fueled fears of a double-dip global recession.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa fell to 3786.75 points, while market volume jumped to 144.77 billion Chilean pesos ($306.5 million), compared with CLP138.02 billion on Friday.\par \par \uc2 With the Ipsa now down nearly 25% from its last closing high of 5040.97 points, hit on Jan. 5, it meets the technical definition of a bear market. A 20% drop from a previous peak points to a bear market.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The Dow plunged 634.76 points as investors scrambled for safer assets.\par \par \uc2 "This is reminiscent of 'Black Monday,' when markets around the world dropped," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with brokerage Molina y Swett. The Ipsa dropped 10.9% as markets around the world crashed on Oct. 19, 1987, so-called Black Monday.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) dropped 7.1% to CLP10,501.00, as airlines the globe over reeled on recession concerns.\par \par \uc2 Shipping company Compania Sud American de Vapores (VAPORES.SN) was also hit by double-dip recession fears, losing 13.9% to CLP210.00. Chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) lost 7.6% to CLP24,450.00, and retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) fell 6.4% to CLP2,550.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended 1.6% weaker against the dollar Monday, at a seven-week low, as the downgrade of U.S. debt sparked risk aversion across global markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso, which ended at CLP472.30 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP464.90, saw its biggest intraday variation since Jan. 4, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP469.00 to CLP474.80.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP471.49 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.60 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended sharply lower as fixed-income participants digested the downgrade of U.S. debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.60%, from 2.68% Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.64%, from 2.76% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 08-08-11 2019GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110808e788001l2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\p