\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 1.4% Higher, Investors Seek Bargains\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2011\par 22:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 1.4% higher Monday, lifted by the initial momentum of soaring U.S. markets, then sustained as investors sought bargains following recent sharp losses.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa rose to 4487.09 points, while market volume slipped to 80.19 billion Chilean pesos ($175.5 million) from CLP88.06 billion in the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavyweights also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 In early trading, the DJIA surged as a debt-ceiling deal reached over the weekend fueled investor appetite, but then turned negative after disappointing Institute for Supply Management manufacturing data.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa, however, held onto most of its early gains as investors went bargain hunting and looked forward to more local quarterly earnings reports.\par \par \uc2 "The local market has been punished too harshly lately, and investors see that. Also, participants are awaiting the [quarterly] results of the retail sector," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Retailers have been pressured lower lately by investigations into alleged fraud committed by department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN).\par \par \uc2 Among them, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) rose 2.5% to CLP3,090.00; department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) jumped 1.1% to CLP4,490.00; and retailer Hites (HITES.SN) increased 0.9% to CLP480.00.\par \par \uc2 For its part, La Polar jumped 7.0% to CLP546.00.\par \par \uc2 Among other gainers, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) expanded 3.4% to CLP12,450.00 after it confirmed it will receive delivery of the first \uc2 Boeing Co\uc2 . (BA) 787-8 Dreamliner passenger jets it purchased in the second half 2012. LAN will be the first Latin American airline to receive delivery of the Dreamliners, which have faced long production and delivery delays.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended stronger against the dollar, despite falling international copper prices, as institutional investors sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP456.90 to the dollar, nearing a three-year high, compared with Friday's close of CLP457.50. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP455.60 to CLP460.00.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP457.18 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.35 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mildly lower as fixed-income market participants digested events unfolding in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.74%, from 2.75% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.87%, from 2.88% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 01-08-11 2020GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110801e781001cr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
