\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Weaker As Institutional Investors Buy Dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2011\par 20:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended weaker against the dollar Friday as institutional investors bought greenbacks following the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent string of three-year-highs.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP457.50 to the dollar, compared with Thursday's close of CLP456.30. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP456.50 to CLP458.80.\par \par \uc2 Despite the dollar's fall versus the euro on weaker-than-expected second quarter U.S. growth data and the ongoing debt-ceiling debacle in the world's largest economy, the peso weakened as investors bought dollars.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 With the peso at its recent three-year highs, "investors closed their short positions ahead of the weekend and bought dollars," said Osvaldo Molina, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at local brokerage and investment bank LarrainVial.\par \par \uc2 In any case, traders and analysts say all eyes are focused on U.S. lawmakers' thus-far fruitless attempts to raise the borrowing limit before Aug. 2.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP457.10 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.30 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as fixed-income market participants watched the events unfolding in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged on the day at 2.75%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.88%, from 2.89% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 29-07-11 1802GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110729e77t001s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
