\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Strong copper, weak dlr to keep Chile peso at highs\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2011\par 20:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Strong copper, weak dollar maintain peso near 3-yr highs\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen out of options to stem surge\par \par \uc2 By Alexandra Ulmer\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, July 29 (Reuters) - Chile's peso <CLP=CL> is likely to remain around three-year highs, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen powerless in the face of soaring prices for copper, the country's main export, and the dollar sagging on U.S. economic and debt woes.\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened 0.26 percent to close at 457.70 on Friday, just a whisker away from the over-three-year intraday high of 455.40 hit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Copper prices spiked to a three-month high early on Friday, driven up by a strike at Chile's giant Escondida mine, before paring gains. The peso often moves in tandem with prices for copper, which accounts for over half of Chilean exports.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was under pressure on fears of a looming U.S. debt default, keeping the peso strong after it broke key resistance at 460 per U.S. dollar this week. However, some analysts say weak U.S. economic data will likely drag on the dollar even if a U.S. default is averted.\par \par \uc2 "It's pretty hard for Chilean authorities to do anything to stop the dollar's fall," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surge comes despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holding its key rate steady in July for the first time in six months, seen by some as bid by the bank to weaken it. [ID:nN1E76C231]\par \par \uc2 It is also defying an ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program aimed at sapping the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that suggests Chile is running out of options to stem a rally that is also hitting most of its regional neighbors. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ > For a TAKE A LOOK on Chile economy [ID:nN26HILEFI] > Americas indicators graphic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/hyt39r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/hyt39r }}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Latin America are rallying on massive dollar inflows triggered by the widening economic growth and rate differentials with the United States and Europe, though the emerging market nations have responded to the surge differently.\par \par \uc2 South American nations will work together to fight hot money from abroad that is pressuring their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Colombian President Juan Manuel Santos said on Thursday after a Union of South American Nations (UNASUR) meeting in Lima. [ID:nN1E76R2B8]\par \par \uc2 But many analysts are skeptical the region has the tools to put the brakes on their strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For all the measures Brazil has adopted, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still reaching maximum heights," said Tricio. "The (Chilean) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't going to take any measures."\par \par \uc2 While most analysts do not expect Chile to unveil new measures, many of which are seen as costly and ineffective, some think current tools could be enhanced.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may for instance increase the amount of its daily dollar purchases from the current $50 million as part of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for 2011 launched in January, said Nathan Pincheira, an analyst with Banchile.\par \par \uc2 "It's the most probable of the options, but still very unlikely," he said.\par \par \uc2 Pincheira sees the peso weakening to 470 per dollar by the end of the year as U.S. default fears ease, regardless of whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But others see the peso's appreciation continuing, as fundamentals -- a sinking dollar and high copper prices -- remain constant, potentially boosting it to a record 430 per dollar by the year end, said Cesar Guzman, senior analyst at Inversiones Security.\par \par \uc2 The peso hit a closing peak of 431.20 in March 2008, the strongest level in the past decade.\par \par \uc2 "We don't see anything that could reverse the (peso's) direction," Guzman said.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Alexandra Ulmer; Editing by Simon Gardner and Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (ANALYSIS)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110801e77t001kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
