\par\par \b \uc2 Chilean Peso Ends At New 3-Year High, Despite Dollar's Rally\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2011\par 19:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--After breaking resistance the prior session, Chile's peso plowed into fresh three-year-high territory against the dollar Wednesday, despite the greenback's rally versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at levels not seen since April 2008 at CLP456.50 to the dollar, compared with Tuesday's close of CLP457.40. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP456.30 to CLP458.20.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latent euro-zone debt worries pushed the euro lower versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Despite specific days in which the dollar rallies, the overall trend we're seeing, especially if U.S. leaders can't agree on raising the debt ceiling, is that the dollar is moving lower against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the globe," said Gloria Soto, head trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 Also, the peso ignored Brazilian authorities' latest measures to tame the rapidly appreciating real.\par \par \uc2 The move, however, highlights that the dollar's broad weakness could again "bring global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars to the front lines," said Sergio Tricio, head of studies with \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Wednesday at an average rate of CLP457.96 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.20 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest poll of financial market traders sees Chile's consumer price index likely increasing 0.1% on the month in July. The previous estimate saw CPI gaining 0.2% in July.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.74%, from 2.71% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged on the day at 2.90%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 27-07-11 1751GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110727e77r001i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
