\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher; Heavily Weighted Commodities Firms Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2011\par 22:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended mildly higher Friday, supported by heavily weighted commodities-related companies recovering from recent losses.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa rose 0.2% to 4627.80 points, while market volume fell to 60.49 billion Chilean pesos ($131.1 million), compared with CLP77.61 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Among commodities-related companies, which have been falling amid a broader market retreat, integrated steel and iron ore producer Cap (CAP.SN) had fallen 2.0% over the last week, while fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN) had slipped 4.7% over the prior seven days.\par \par \uc2 "Companies like Copec and Cap have seen their share prices punished heavily of late and are looking attractive now," said a local analyst, who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 Cap jumped 1.8% to CLP22,044.00 and Copec gained 2.2% to CLP8,372.50.\par \par \uc2 Also, chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) rose 0.3% to CLP30,700.00. Earlier this week, local investment bank and brokerage LarrainVial gave SQM a buy recommendation and a 12-to-18-month target price of CLP34,600.\par \par \uc2 The three companies have a 22% weighting on the Ipsa.\par \par \uc2 Also gaining, specialty branded generic drugs manufacturer \uc2 Corporacion Farmaceutica Recalcine\uc2 's (CFR.SN) shares surged 6.6% to CLP117.01 as the company continues to expand in neighboring Argentina.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended slightly weaker versus the dollar as institutional investors bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as initial enthusiasm about a bailout proposal for Greece waned, pressuring the euro lower.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP461.30 to the dollar, compared with its three-month high of CLP460.70 on Thursday, while trading in a range of CLP460.50 to CLP462.30.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for European ports, the peso often tracks the euro's movements against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP461.81 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7.05 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in light over-the-counter trading.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged on the day at 2.72%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.89%, from 2.90% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 22-07-11 2036GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110722e77m0017h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
