\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher On Optimism About Euro, US Debt Deals\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2011\par 22:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Thursday as optimism European Union leaders could stem a brewing sovereign debt crisis and hopes for a major budget deal in the U.S. lifted risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa grew 0.3% to 4618.04 points, while market volume slipped to 77.61 billion Chilean pesos ($168.5 million), compared with CLP82.28 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The DJIA surged 152.50 points, ending 1.2% higher at 12724.41 points on hopes that authorities on both sides of the Atlantic would reach deals on their respective debt problems.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) rose 0.5% to CLP13,276; bank \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2  (SAN, BSANTANDE.SN) gained 0.9% to CLP41.99; and energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) climbed 0.5% to CLP211.\par \par \uc2 Also, retailers were among the session's biggest gainers, recovering part of their losses in recent weeks. Retailers have been reeling as department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) is investigated for alleged fraud and participants anticipate tougher regulations for credit-card-issuing retailers to be implemented.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) increased 0.5% to CLP3,142.40, department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) jumped 1.2% to CLP4,637, retailer Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) gained 1.3% to CLP544.776.\par \par \uc2 La Polar, however, dropped 8.3% to a 52-week low of CLP459.59.\par \par \uc2 "There are solid companies in Chile, but their share prices, especially the retail sector, has been punished of late because of the ongoing investigations of La Polar," said Marcelo Catalan, analyst with brokerage BCI Corrdedor de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended at a three-month high Thursday, boosted by a rising euro as European Union leaders sought ways to reduce Greece's debt burden and avoid spillover effects to other member nations.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP460.70 to the dollar, compared with CLP462.60 on Wednesday, while trading in a range of CLP460.70 to CLP463.20.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Thursday at an average rate of CLP462.86 to the dollar. It has accumulated $7 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in a thin trading session.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.72%, from 2.73% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.90%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 21-07-11 2033GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110721e77l001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
