\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 1.3% Lower As La Polar Still Weighs On Market\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2011\par 22:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 1.3% lower Wednesday, led lower by retailers which are feeling the sting of allegations of fraud committed by department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) and the Sernac consumer-rights authority's lawsuit against \uc2 Wal-Mart Stores\uc2 ' (WMT) Chilean unit.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa declined to 4601.06 points, while market volume rose 82.28 billion Chilean pesos ($177.9 million), compared with CLP78.58 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several weeks, the government and regulatory authorities have been investigating La Polar for allegedly hiding past-due payments on the company's books and purportedly handing regulators false information.\par \par \uc2 The local SVS securities regulator will reportedly hold up La Polar's $200 million capital increase, which shareholders recently approved and the company's newly appointed president said is absolutely necessary for the company's survival, until the company hands in a newly revised and audited version of its financial report.\par \par \uc2 Also, the Sernac consumer-rights watchdog served \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2 's Chilean unit a class-action lawsuit for irregularities regarding how it reports clients to credit-reporting agency Dicom.\par \par \uc2 "All that sort of news will definitely hurt sentiment in the market," said a local analyst, who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN), whose chief financial officer recently resigned, shed 2.6% to CLP3,128.10. Also, department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) lost 1.6% to CLP4,581.00; retailer Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) fell 1.3% to CLP538.06; and La Polar dropped 4.9% to CLP501.03.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended weaker against the dollar, erasing its earlier gains and moving away from three-year highs as it tracked slumping international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP462.60 to the dollar, compared with CLP461.90 on Tuesday, while trading in a range of CLP460.80 to CLP463.80.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Wednesday at an average rate of CLP463.51 to the dollar. It has accumulated $6.95 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's scheduled auction of sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.73%, off from 2.75% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.90%, up from 2.89% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 20-07-11 2022GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110720e77k0018y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
