\par\par \b \uc2 Chile's Peso Closes Weaker Following  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Rate Pause\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2011\par 20:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended weaker versus the dollar Friday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in line with expectations, kept the benchmark overnight rate steady after market close the prior session.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP462.40 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP461.70, while trading in a range of CLP461.30 to CLP462.95.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped despite the euro's gains versus the dollar following the results of the latest stress-test results on euro-zone banks and despite rising international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 As nearly a third of Chile's exports are bound for European ports and because the nation is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for a third of global supply, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar and usually takes trading cues from the red metal's international prices.\par \par \uc2 As inflationary pressures and expectations have eased, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the benchmark rate at 5.25% late Thursday, its first rate-hike pause in six months.\par \par \uc2 Although the move was widely expected, it left the peso with room to weaken, and prompted "local traders to boost their dollar positions before the weekend," said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP461.95 to the dollar, having accumulated $6.80 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept rates pat.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.74%, from 2.73% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.89%, from 2.90% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 15-07-11 1806GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110715e77f0013f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
