\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close Lower As Hopes For New US Stimulus Thwarted\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended lower Thursday, tracking slumping U.S. markets, as Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said there aren't any plans to introduce another round of quantitative easing and concerns persisted about Europe's fiscal health.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa fell 0.61% to 4695.46 points, while market volume slipped to 75.79 billion Chilean pesos ($164.2 million), from CLP99.6 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The DJIA ended 54.49 points, or 0.44%, lower at 12437.12 points as the Fed chief's comments deflated investors' stimulus hopes and despite signs of possible progress in Washington's debt negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) declined 1.0% to CLP13,600.00, chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) fell 1.2% to CLP29,900.00, and bank \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  (BCH, CHILE.SN) declined 0.7% to CLP68.50.\par \par \uc2 Retailers again were among the biggest decliners in the wake of department store La Polar's (LAPOLAR.SN) disclosure last month that it overcharged its clients for past-due credit-card bills and said it needed to reserve $890 million to cover bad loans. La Polar's questionable business practices, which allegedly include hiding past-due payments on the company's books and handing regulators false information, have cast a cloud of uncertainty over the retail sector.\par \par \uc2 La Polar slipped 0.3% to CLP555.00, retail holding company \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) fell 0.7% to CLP3,251.00, and department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) decreased 0.9% to CLP4,650.00.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the government's planned auction of most of its stakes in the Essbio SA (ESSBIO-A.SN) utility operating in southern Chile and the Esval SA (ESVAL-A.SN) utility in the port of Valparaiso likely contributed to the Ipsa's fall.\par \par \uc2 Market participants likely cashed in shares to participate in the auction, which is scheduled to take place on the Santiago Stock Exchange on Friday morning, said Alfredo Parra, an analyst at brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, despite a falling euro, slipping copper prices and expectations for the Andean nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep interest rates steady later in the session, as institutional investors sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP461.70 to the dollar, versus Wednesday's close of CLP462.65, while trading in a range of CLP460.80 to CLP463.10.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Thursday at an average rate of CLP462.65 to the dollar, having accumulated $6.75 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower as fixed-income market participants expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the benchmark overnight rate at 5.25% at its monthly monetary policy meeting after market close.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.73%, down from 2.77% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.90%, down from 2.92% 