\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Mildly Stronger As Euro, Copper Prices Recover\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2011\par 20:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended mildly stronger versus the dollar Tuesday as international copper prices regained some lost ground, although continued worries about euro zone debt contagion kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining further.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP466.90 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP467.20, while trading in a range of CLP466.60 to CLP468.50.\par \par \uc2 With Chile the world's largest copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Three-month copper on the London Metal Exchange traded 0.8% higher at $9,650 a metric ton as previously bearish investors were forced to buy back short positions and as the dollar weakened slightly against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The peso has been tracking copper's rise and fall very closely in recent sessions, but concerns about Europe's debt crisis are still the focus of much attention," said Flavio Magnasco, trader with bank Banco Falabella.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is facing a strong level of support at CLP467.50-CLP468.50, and will likely not break that level if copper prices stay strong or the euro recovers, said Magnasco.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Tuesday at an average rate of CLP468.22 to the dollar, having accumulated $6.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as private inflation expectations continue to come down.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index is expected to increase 4% on the year--within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3%, plus or minus 1 percentage point--according to the median forecast of 66 local analysts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly economic outlook survey published earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.75%, from 2.74% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.91%, from 2.95% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by ValorFuturo newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 12-07-11 1813GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110712e77c0018f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
