\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends At 2-Week High As Euro, Copper Rise On Greece\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2011\par 20:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended at a two-week high versus the dollar Wednesday, as the euro jumped against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and international copper prices surged after Greece's parliament approved a five-year austerity plan.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP469.60 to the dollar, compared with CLP472.60 on Tuesday, while trading in a range of CLP469.60 to CLP472.30.\par \par \uc2 The peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar because Chile's economy is highly trade-dependent and nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for European ports.\par \par \uc2 While the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared back some of its earlier gains after the austerity vote, it was still trading higher versus the greenback Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Three-month copper on the London Metal Exchange, meanwhile, ended at an eight-week high after the Greek vote enticed risk appetite. It closed up 2.7% at $9,320 per ton.\par \par \uc2 "With improved market sentiment and with copper [prices] firmly above $4.00 per pound again, the peso regained nearly half of what it had lost in the prior two weeks in only one session," said Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 According to Chile's state copper commission Cochilco, spot copper ended higher at $4.16216 per pound on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million on Wednesday at an average rate of CLP471.42 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $6.2 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher again as fixed-income participants kept their eyes on headlines from Europe.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.69%, from 2.67% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.94%, versus 2.92% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 29-06-11 1802GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110629e76t0017r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
