\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 1.4% Higher, Tracks US Markets, Retail Leads\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2011\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 1.4% higher Tuesday, tracking surging U.S markets. Local retailing issues jumped after local businessman Alvaro Saieh disclosed that he acquired a controlling 10% stake in financially troubled department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN)\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa ended higher at 4762.99 points, while market volume jumped to 111.2 billion Chilean pesos ($235.3 million), from CLP67.3 billion on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, markets, banks, businesses and government offices were closed in Chile in observance of St. Peter's and St. Paul's Day.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 The DJIA finished 1.2% higher At 12188.69 points, as investors warmed to risk assets amid signs of progress in Greece's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) gained 1.6% to CLP13,180.00; specialty fertilizer and chemical producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B series (SQM-B.SN) rose 1.3% to CLP29,540.00; and bank \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2  (SAN, BSANTANDE.SN) jumped 2.3% to CLP42.20.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, retailer's shares surged after Saieh, who already has controlling stakes in the local Unimarc supermarket chain, La Tercera newspaper and \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  SA (BCA, CORPBANCA.SN), said he bought a 10% stake in La Polar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, La Polar disclosed that it had overcharged its credit-card customers and would need to set aside some $900 million to cover bad loans to those customers.\par \par \uc2 La Polar allegedly raised interest rates, charged delinquent fees to more than 400,000 clients without negotiating new contract terms with them and handed regulators false information.\par \par \uc2 La Polar jumped 16.7% to CLP736.00, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) increased 2.6% to CLP3,389.00, department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) gained 0.9% to CLP4,850.00 and rival Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) climbed 1.7% to CLP587.00.\par \par \uc2 "It's still too early to tell what's Saieh's real intentions are with La Polar--he might just be looking to make a quick buck. Either way, that a seasoned businessman like him bough a chunk in La Polar is boosting the sector's share prices," said a local analyst who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar as optimism that Greek authorities will strike an agreement on austerity measures boosted the euro against the dollar and lifted international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP472.60 to the dollar, compared with CLP473.70 on Thursday, while trading in a tight range of CLP472.60 to CLP473.50.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million on Tuesday at an average rate of CLP473.47 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $6.15 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher in a thin trading session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 28-06-11 2019GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 D