\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close Higher, Get A Lift From Electricity Sector\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2011\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Friday, boosted by power generators as they benefit from safe-haven buying.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa ended 0.2% higher at 4701.70 points, while market volume slipped to 67.3 billion Chilean pesos ($142.1 million), versus an unusually high CLP218.2 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Volume was high on Thursday as health-care company \uc2 Cruz Blanca Salud\uc2  (CRUZBLANCA.SN) debuted on the Santiago Stock Exchange, listing 222.1 million shares at CLP500 each and raising $233.8 million. In its second day of trading, \uc2 Cruz Blanca Salud\uc2 's shares lost 2% to CLP487.98.\par \par \uc2 Power generators, whose shares have lagged behind other sectors, gained as "they electricity generation industry is seen as a safer bet and investors seek refuge in them, when there's a lot of uncertainty in market," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Greece's ongoing debt saga and fears about euro-zone contagion have dragged international markets lower in recent days.\par \par \uc2 The nation's largest power generator by installed capacity, \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN), climbed 1.7% to CLP890.00, while its parent company, power holding firm \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) rose 0.9% to CLP216.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, pulp-and-paper producer CMPC (CMPC.SN) gained 1.5% to CLP24,400.00 after local bank \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2  earlier this week gave the company a CLP31,000, 12-month price target.\par \par \uc2 In other local market news, the peso ended slightly stronger against the dollar on the back of rising international copper prices, although it pared back earlier gains as euro-zone fears resurfaced.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP473.70 to the dollar, compared with CLP474.20 in the prior session, while trading in a tight range of CLP472.15 to CLP474.20.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP473.95 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $6.10 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher after Finance Minister Felipe Larrain reiterated on Thursday that inflationary pressures are easing.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  revised its 2011 inflation outlook to 4% from 4.3% on lower international food and fuel prices.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.64%, up from 2.62% Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.91%, versus 2.90% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Markets, banks, businesses and government offices will be closed in Chile on Monday in observance of a religious holiday.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 24-06-11 2018GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110624e76o0012n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
