\par\par \b \uc2 Chile's Peso, Other Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Prepare To Go Global\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2011\par 18:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Moves in bond markets seen as early steps to make Chile's peso deliverable\par \par \uc2 --Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market seen becoming more liquid\par \par \uc2 --Other emerging market countries also opening up bond markets\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Chile is preparing to gate-crash the small club of emerging-market countries whose \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are fully accessible to international investors anywhere.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The drive to make the peso deliverable, or easy to trade and access offshore, has begun. In an early step, the country recently said Euroclear, a global provider of cross-border settlement services, will begin operating in Chile to help foreign investors access the local fixed-income market. In another step to make the peso deliverable, Chile's government recently eased restrictions on peso-denominated bonds issued by foreigners.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among a growing field of emerging-market nations that are liberalizing their bond markets and setting their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the path to full, international convertibility, Chile is seen as a leader. That step is expected to assure it of financing gains as the added market liquidity in its markets are expected to narrow interest rate spreads and reduce execution costs for investors. But Chile will also have to live with a potentially more volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during periods of global turmoil.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which currently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to manage the peso's value, may have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less as its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  becomes convertible, says RBC strategist Eduardo Suarez. The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market would be deeper and it would be harder for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or any one player, to influence the market. Suarez says, though, that the added liquidity will be a "long-term tailwind" for the peso.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  convertibility might also help Chile, a big copper producer, solidify its base in international trade, says IDEAGlobal strategist Enrique Alvarez.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 International investors currently have restricted access to most emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and trade them via derivatives called nondeliverable forwards. If these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  become deliverable, international banks could hold them as assets offshore and the market for these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would become more liquid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The experiences of the other three freely accessible emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --the Mexican peso, the South African rand and the Turkish lira--suggest it may take a few years for Chile to join them. RBC's Suarez says Mexico's peso took three or four years to be deliverable from the time Euroclear started operating there.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even countries with a history of strict capital controls such as India have started loosening bond market restrictions, with implications for their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The rupee isn't expected to be fully convertible anytime soon, but Ravi Chachra, chief investment officer of Eight Capital, an India-focused credit fund, points to India's moves to increase the limits for foreign investors investing in local bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As India's bond market grows "the money is going to be flowing in and out in dollars," says Chachra, adding that could imply a "ten-fold boost" in trading in the rupee.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adrian Lee, president of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management firm Lee Overlay Partners says \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Russian ruble are also on the path to become deliverable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Of course, the elephant in the room remains China's yuan, still a tightly controlled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If China allows the yuan to become convertible, other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Indian rupee might follow suit, Lee says. That may still be some way off.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com [ 06-22-11 1255ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110622e76m000d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
