\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher On Retailers, Even As La Polar Drops\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2011\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Monday, as retail-sector shares recovered from their recent sharp losses, even as department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) plummeted.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa ended 0.1% higher at 4628.48 points, while volume slipped to 115.6 billion Chilean pesos ($244.9 million), compared to CLP154.4 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 La Polar dropped 63.4% to CLP523.00 following a one-week trading suspension after the retailer disclosed what it called "unorthodox practices" in its in-store credit-card department.\par \par \uc2 La Polar said last week that it will have to set aside almost $900 million to cover the past-due loans its credit-card department made to customers.\par \par \uc2 Retail-sector shares reeled in recent session as investors expected the separate investigations by the national prosecutor's office, congress, and the banking, securities and pension fund regulators into La Polar's shady business practices to usher in tougher regulations for credit-card issuers.\par \par \uc2 In Chile, roughly 50% of department store clients pay for their purchases with in-store credit cards. Despite the fact that department stores offer credit, these credit issues aren't regulated by the banking overseer.\par \par \uc2 "The retail sector is recovering after being punished much too harshly last week," said Rodolfo Tapia, analyst with bank Banco Penta.\par \par \uc2 Retailers also jumped as participants speculated one of the nation's larger retailers could move to acquire La Polar.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, retail holding \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) rose 5.0% to CLP3,421.10; department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) jumped 6.9% to CLP4,827.30; retailer Hites (HITES.SN) gained 6.5% to CLP559.08; and rival Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) climbed 3.8% to CLP557.63.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended virtually flat versus the dollar, paring its earlier losses, as the euro recovered against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on aid hopes for debt-laden Greece.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP472.00 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close at CLP471.90, after trading in a tight range of CLP473.90 to CLP472.00.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP473.77 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.90 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged in light trading as fixed-income participants awaited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly monetary policy report scheduled for release later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended without variation at 2.63%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.92%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 20-06-11 2029GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110620e76k0016i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
