\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Flat On S&P Greece Downgrade, US Market Slump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2011\par 20:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended flat against the dollar Monday, as \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgrade of Greece, falling U.S. markets, and slumping international copper prices, sapped the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's earlier strength.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP467.60 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close at CLP467.50, after trading in a narrow range of CLP466.20 to CLP468.35.\par \par \uc2 Market sentiment went sour after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  slashed its ratings on Greece another three notches on its expectations that the likelihood of one or more defaults over the next 12 months is significantly higher amid efforts by its creditors to close an emerging financing gap.\par \par \uc2 Also, U.S. stocks shed their morning gains on concerns about the health of economy, helping to pull the peso back from its previous gains.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average, which was recently down 0.1%, is often looked at to gauge risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, as Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for a third of the global supply, the peso also often takes trading cues from moves in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Copper in London fell 0.3% from Friday to $8,910 a metric ton in a largely directionless trading session.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP465.85 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged in a thin trading session, as participants awaited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase the benchmark overnight rate by 25 basis points at its next monthly monetary policy meeting scheduled for Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release its post-meeting communique after 2200 GMT Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, unchanged from Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged on the day at 2.91%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 13-06-11 1806GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110613e76d0010j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
