\par\par \b \uc2 Chilean Peso Closes Weaker Tracking Slump In London Copper\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2011\par 19:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended weaker against the dollar Friday, tracking the tumble copper prices took on the London Metal Exchange.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP467.50 to the dollar, compared with Thursday's close at CLP466.30, after trading in a narrow range of CLP467.50 to CLP468.80.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for a third of the global supply, the peso also often takes trading cues from moves in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 LME three-month copper fell 1.3% from Thursday amid a broad-based selloff in commodities on the back of weaker-than-expected Chinese import data and safe-haven dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 A retreating euro following European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet's comments Thursday also contributed to the peso's decline. Trichet refused to commit to a sustained monetary-policy-tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2 With a third of Chile's exports going to Europe, the peso often moves in the same direction the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP468.20 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.6 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged in a quiet session.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, unchanged from Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.91%, also unchanged from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 10-06-11 1747GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110610e76a0014q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
