\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Mildly Higher As Retailers Rebound From Slump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2011\par 22:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended mildly higher Tuesday, as heavy-weighted retailers recovered some of the sharp losses posted the prior session.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa closed 0.1% higher at 4815.40 points, while market volume grew to 92.8 billion Chilean pesos ($199.1 million) from CLP65.0 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Chilean retailers with \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Peru posted steep drops the prior session after left-wing nationalist Ollanta Humala was elected Peru's president in a run-off vote on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Among rebounding shares, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) gained 0.2% to CLP3,463.00, department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) increased 0.2% to CLP5,170.10 and mall operator and developer Parque Arauco (PARAUCO.SN) jumped 0.8% to CLP1,149.60.\par \par \uc2 "After tumbling sharply on Monday, its no surprise that retailers with exposure to Peru are recovering, even if only slightly, today," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Also, the Ipsa pared back some of its gains late in the session after downbeat comments by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke.\par \par \uc2 Among decliners, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) lost 0.6% to CLP13,075.00 after it cancelled or delayed many of its flights to and from Argentina because of the presence of volcanic ash.\par \par \uc2 LAN said it is gradually restarting flights to and from Argentina's busiest airports, Ezeiza and Aeroparque, even though Chile's Puyehue volcano continues to spew tons of ash into the atmosphere after erupting over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, tracking the euro's rise to a one-month high against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The peso finished at CLP466.20 to the dollar, compared with Monday's close at CLP468.20, after trading in a range of CLP466.20 to CLP467.90.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , purchased $50 million Tuesday at an average rate of CLP467.40 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.45 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as participants awaited consumer price index data for the month of May.\par \par \uc2 Participants expect the CPI to increase 0.3% on the month in May when the government statistics agency releases the information early Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, from 2.60% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.90%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 07-06-11 2028GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110607e767001g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
