\par\par \b \uc2 Chile's Peso Closes Weaker On Lower-Than-Expected Growth Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2011\par 20:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended slightly weaker against the dollar Monday on lower-than-expected economic growth data and the dollar's gains versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP468.20 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close at CLP467.70, after trading in a range of CLP467.50 to CLP469.00.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped after Chile's monthly economic activity index, or Imacec, grew 6.3% on the year in April, marginally below the market consensus for a 6.5% increase.\par \par \uc2 Also, as Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for Europe, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro slid mildly against the dollar from a one-month high on concerns about the European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of disappointing Imacec data and a slightly stronger dollar internationally, helped to pull back the peso," said Sergio Tricio, head of studies with local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in the coming weeks, investor anxiety about the election of left-wing nationalist Ollanta Humala in neighboring Peru may seep into Chile and weaken the peso, Tricio said.\par \par \uc2 "That hasn't happened yet, but if investors become really spooked we could see a knee-jerk effect across the region and investments being pulled. That would ultimately weaken the peso," he said.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP467.80 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.40 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as participants geared up for state-owned bank BancoEstado's and shopping center operator Mall Plaza's bond issue scheduled for Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged at 2.60%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.90%, up from 2.88% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 06-06-11 1811GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110606e766000y1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
