\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Slightly Higher; Power Sector Surges\b0\par\par\uc2 By Renzo Dasso   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2011\par 22:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended modestly higher Monday amid low volume on the U.S. holiday, with energy-sector shares standing out as the ghost of power rationing fades.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa closed 0.1% higher at 4847.15 points, while market volume fell to an unusually low 48.8 billion Chilean pesos ($104.4 million), from CLP65.8 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Declines were led by retailer La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN), which fell 3.1% to CLP2,514.70 in reaction to a $400 million capital increase announcement late Friday. Analysts say there is a degree of uncertainty regarding La Polar's financial health, following its earnings report for the fourth quarter of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Retail shares, which saw sharp gains recently on strong domestic demand expectations, were dragged down by La Polar's performance, said local brokerage Cruz del Sur analyst Paulina Barahona.\par \par \uc2 "La Polar influenced the retail sector's decline, which also saw profit taking following last week's surge," she added.\par \par \uc2 The nation's largest department store, Falabella (FALABELLA.SN), decreased 0.7% to CLP5,153.00 and retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) shed 0.9% to CLP3,538.00. Rival department store chain Ripley fell 0.9% to CLP649.10.\par \par \uc2 Power sector companies, meanwhile, led the gains following reports of increased water levels in the country's reservoirs, which calms fears of rationing and shows increased availability of hydrogeneration.\par \par \uc2 The country's largest power generator \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) advanced 0.9% to CLP1,353.70. Its parent company energy holding \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) gained 0.7% to CLP204.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, Chile's peso ended marginally weaker against the dollar Monday, in a directionless session on the holidays in the U.S. and the U.K.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP467.00 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP466.60, after trading in a narrow range of CLP466.80 to CLP468.30.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP467.73 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.15 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower amid thin, interbank trading, as the market awaits a scheduled sovereign bond auction by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.61%, from 2.63% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.88%, versus 2.91% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Renzo Dasso, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; renzo.dasso@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Carolina Pica contributes to this article. [ 30-05-11 2044GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110530e75u000uj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
