\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso End Marginally Weaker In Directionless Session\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2011\par 19:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended marginally weaker against the dollar Monday, in a directionless session on the holidays in the U.S. and the U.K.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP467.00 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP466.60, after trading in a narrow range of CLP466.80 to CLP468.30.\par \par \uc2 Memorial Day in the U.S. left the peso bereft of several indicators it usually takes direction from, such as the Dow Jones Industrial Average and the dollar in U.S. markets, and the U.K.'s Spring Bank Holiday deprived it of London copper prices.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, the peso often takes trading cues from the metal's price. Additionally, market volume was low, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't react to the industrial production data released at the start of the session as the 9.5% on-year increase for the month of April was in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP467.73 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.15 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower amid thin, interbank trading, as the market awaits a scheduled sovereign bond auction by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.61%, from 2.63% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.88%, versus 2.91% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 30-05-11 1750GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110530e75u000to\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
