\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Closes Stronger On OECD GDP Forecast, Copper Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2011\par 19:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended slightly stronger versus the dollar Wednesday, as the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development sees the Andean nation's gross domestic product expanding 6.5% in 2011 and as international copper prices again broke above $9,000 a metric ton.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP471.40 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP471.60, while trading in a range of CLP470.20 to CLP473.10.\par \par \uc2 The OECD, a Paris-based think tank, also said it expects domestic demand to grow 9% in 2011. Its forecast for GDP growth is on the upper end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's expectations for a 5.5%-6.5% expansion, and above the bank's forecast for 7.6% growth of domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 "Strong economic growth and continued robust domestic demand will support more interest rate hikes, which is what has boosted the peso [versus the dollar]," said Matias Pizarro, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  head at local bank \uc2 Banco Security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The benchmark overnight rate is now at 5% and is expected to be raised to 6% by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Also, since Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, accounting for a third of global supply, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Copper for three-month delivery gained 2.3% on the London Metal Exchange at $9,065 a metric ton, reversing the losses it suffered earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the peso gained as a battered euro pared early losses, as modest demand for higher-yielding assets temporarily outweighed jitters about the euro zone's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of the nation's exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Wednesday at an average rate of CLP470.88. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $5.00 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher following a scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued bonds.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.63%, from 2.61% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.92%, from 2.90% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 25-05-11 1750GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110525e75p00190\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
