\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close Lower, Tracking Falling US Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2011\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended slightly lower on lingering euro-zone debt concerns and as it tracked sliding U.S. markets.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa closed 0.2% lower at 4790.38 points, while market volume jumped to 124.7 billion Chilean pesos ($264.4 million), from CLP64.8 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares are also listed in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 The DJIA ended 0.2% lower at 12356.21 points on weak U.S. manufacturing data.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) slipped 0.2% to CLP13,440.00; energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) lost 0.4% to CLP200.90 and wine maker and exporter Concha y Toro (VCO, CONCHATOR.SN) slid 0.2% to CLP1,175.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, investors were still jittery about Europe's finances following a recent spate of ratings agency warnings, helping to keep the local equity market subdued.\par \par \uc2 "Folks are still worried about what's happening in Europe, that countries like Greece might not renegotiate their debt," said Rodolfo Tapia, analyst at local bank Banco Penta.\par \par \uc2 Also declining, retailer La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) shed 1.4% to CLP2,602.10 and fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN) decreased 1.2% to CLP8,545.70\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, rebounding from its sharp losses the prior session, as international copper prices and the euro recovered.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP471.60 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP473.00, while trading in a range of CLP470.40 to CLP472.75.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Tuesday at an average rate of CLP471.39. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.95 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as fixed-income market participants awaited an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued bonds, scheduled for Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged on the day at 2.61%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.90%, from 2.88% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 24-05-11 2032GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110524e75o0019h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
