\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Comments Lift Retailers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2011\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended slightly higher Friday as retailers surged after the central pointed to a more moderate pace of future rate increases.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa closed 0.1% higher at 4818.96 points, while market volume slimmed to 210.0 billion Chilean pesos ($450.1 million), from CLP310.8 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 Trading in bank \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  (BCA, CORPBANCA.SN) accounted for nearly half of volume Friday, after a 6.3% stake in the company, worth $225 million, was sold.\par \par \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  ended 1.3% higher at CLP7.45, after 14.4 billion of its shares were sold at CLP7.35 a piece.\par \par \uc2 Retailers jumped after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Jose De Gregorio said that despite strong economic growth the country isn't showing signs of overheating and that in coming monthly monetary-policy meetings, rate rises will likely be smaller than the recent 50-basis-point increases, and there could even be a few pauses.\par \par \uc2 "More moderate rate hikes will support domestic demand, which as recent [gross domestic product] data pointed out, remains strong," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) gained 0.4% to CLP5,030.00, retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) increased 1.9% to CLP3,590.00 and retailer Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) expanded 2.6% to CLP628.00.\par \par \uc2 Falling U.S. markets, however, pulled dually listed shares lower, paring back the Ipsa's gains.\par \par \uc2 Several of the Ipsa's heavier weighted shares are also listed in New York, leading the Ipsa to often track the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 Among dually-listed shares, bank \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  (BCH, CHILE.SN) lost 1.0% to CLP69.00; power producer \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) shed 0.8% to CLP862.00; and flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) declined 0.4% to CLP13,447.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, despite a tumbling euro and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments regarding monetary policy, as international copper prices surged.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended stronger at CLP466.60 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP467.60, while trading in a range of CLP466.50 to CLP470.00.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Friday at an average rate of CLP468.21. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.85 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged in light over-the-counter trading as fixed-income market participants digested De Gregorio's comments.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged at 2.62%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unvaried at 2.89%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 20-05-11 2042GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110520e75k00158\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
