\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher On Strong GDP Data, Rising US Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2011\par 22:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Wednesday, as first-quarter gross domestic product surged higher and U.S. markets rose.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa increased 0.3% to 4865.86 points, while market volume grew to 138.7 billion Chilean pesos ($295.7 million) after 690.9 million shares of bank \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  (BCH, CHILE.SN) were auctioned at CLP68.84 per share. Trading in \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  accounted for nearly 36% of volume. The prior session volume totaled CLP108.2 billion.\par \par \uc2 Chile's GDP leapt 9.8% on the year in the first quarter, in line with analysts' expectations, as the country recovered from a devastating February 2010 earthquake on the back of robust domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 "Shares shot higher from the opening bell after the GDP data," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Among gainers, department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) increased 0.6% to CLP5,049.00, construction company \uc2 Salfacorp\uc2  (SALFACORP.SN) jumped 1.2% to CLP1,826.00 and integrated steel and iron ore producer Cap (CAP.SN) expanded 0.8% to CLP23,150.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, as several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The DJIA closed 80.60 points higher, or 0.7% up, at 12560.18 following the release of the Federal Reserve's minutes, which showed \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are in no hurry to tighten monetary policy even as they held detailed exit-strategy talks.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  climbed 0.3% to CLP69.60, energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) gained 2.4% to CLP208.49 and chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) rose 1.1% to CLP27,000.00.\par \par \uc2 Local participants anxiously awaited salmon and trout producer Empresas AquaChile's debut on the local bourse, scheduled for Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "There's a lot of anticipation surrounding the IPO," said Arriagada\par \par \uc2 AquaChile's intial public offering will be the second on the Santiago Stock Exchange this year.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended 1% stronger versus the dollar, as international copper prices surged and the dollar weakened broadly.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP469.00 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP473.50, while trading in a range of CLP469.00 to CLP474.30.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Wednesday at an average rate of CLP473.21. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.75 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as local private pension fund managers--the nation's biggest institutional investors--bought longer bonds in a scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -issued sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, compared with 2.63% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.87%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929;\par \par \uc2 anthony.esposito@dowjones.com 