\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher, Retailers Jump On Demand Expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2011\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Tuesday, as expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will slow down the pace of interest-rate rises, a move which will support demand, boosted retailers.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa gained 0.7% to 4855.92 points, while market volume jumped to 114.2 billion Chilean pesos ($245.7 million), from CLP71.9 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Local analysts, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest monthly economic-outlook survey, expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow down the rate of interest-rate increases to 25 basis points when it holds its monthly monetary-policy meeting on Thursday. The bank previously increased the rate by a half a percentage point at both of its last monthly meetings.\par \par \uc2 A move to slow down the pace of monetary tightening would support domestic demand and "ultimately propped up retailers, which are very sensitive to this type of news," said Peter McMenamin, analyst with local investment bank Banchile Inversiones.\par \par \uc2 Retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) led the sector with a 3.4% jump to CLP3,619.40. Department store Falabella (FALABELLA.SN) gained 0.5% to CLP5,031.00, while rivals La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) increased 1.8% to CLP2,820.60 and Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) expanded 1.9% to CLP638.05.\par \par \uc2 Also, commodities-related companies gained as data showed China's April trade surplus well outstripped expectations. The figures were viewed as a positive for that China's economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN) climbed 1.0% to CLP9.003.30; pulp and paper producer CMPC (CMPC.SN) increased 1.3% to CLP25,381.00; and integrated steel and iron ore producer Cap (CAP.SN) gained 1.1% to CLP22,958.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, as participants unwound long-dollar positions ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary-policy meeting and as international copper prices continued to rebound.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP464.50 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP467.20, while trading in a range of CLP464.50 to CLP466.50.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million on Tuesday at an average rate of CLP466.11. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.45 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher in light over-the-counter trading as analysts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly economic outlook survey also saw the consumer price index likely increasing 4.3% in 2011 from 2010.\par \par \uc2 The outlook, in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.3% year-end inflation outlook, is slightly lower than the 4.4% year-end inflation expectation seen in last month's poll.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.59%, from 2.58% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.91%, versus 2.88% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929;\par \par \uc2 anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 10-05-11 2040GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110510e75a001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
