\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Firmer On Rate Hike Expectations, Copper Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2011\par 19:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended stronger versus the dollar Tuesday, as participants unwound long-dollar positions ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting on Thursday and as international copper prices continued to rebound.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP464.50 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP467.20, while trading in a range of CLP464.50 to CLP466.50.\par \par \uc2 The peso rose as market participants were still divided as to whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase the benchmark overnight interest rate 25 basis points or 50 basis points from its current 4.5% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Also, spot copper prices in London trading rose 0.3% to $4.05308 per pound, according to Chile's state copper commission Cochilco, as investors cautiously eyed key Chinese inflation data.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile is the world's largest copper producer, accounting for a third of global output, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often takes direction from the industrial metal's prices abroad.\par \par \uc2 "A combination of increasing copper prices, which boosted emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and expectations for another rate hike later this week are boosting the peso," said Andres Perez, trader with local brokerage Valores Security.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million on Tuesday at an average rate of CLP466.11. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.45 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher in light over-the-counter trading as local analysts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest monthly economic outlook survey see the consumer price index likely increasing 4.3% in 2011 from 2010.\par \par \uc2 The outlook, in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.3% year-end inflation outlook, is slightly lower than the 4.4% year-end inflation expectation seen in last month's poll.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.59%, from 2.58% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.91%, versus 2.88% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 10-05-11 1748GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110510e75a001f7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
