\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher As \uc2 Endesa\uc2 ,Colbun Rise On HidroAysen Vote\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2011\par 22:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index closed higher Monday, as power generators \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) and \uc2 Colbun (COLBUN.SN) \uc2 surged on expectations that environmental authorities will approve their joint-venture HidroAysen hydroelectric power project.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa rose 0.1% to 4818.61 points, while market volume slipped to 71.9 billion Chilean pesos ($153.9 million), from CLP104.2 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 With participants largely expecting environmental authorities to approve the $3.2 billion, 2,750 megawatt generation project--Chile's biggest in terms of installed capacity once built--shares of Colbun and \uc2 Endesa\uc2  jumped. Voting is scheduled to be complete after market close Monday.\par \par \uc2 "At this point, it's pure speculation that the project will be approved, but that's what is fueling \uc2 Endesa\uc2 's and Colbun's shares," said Rodridgo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina Y Swett.\par \par \uc2 Endesa\uc2  gained 1.8% to CLP892.00 and Colbun increased 0.9% to CLP143.10.\par \par \uc2 Retailers, 1which are expected to continue benefiting from strong domestic demand, were also among the session's biggest winners.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, department store La Polar (LAPOLAR.SN) rose 3.3% to CLP2,778.00, while rivals Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) rose 2.3% to CLP633.00 and Hites (HITES.SN) climbed 1.7% to CLP712.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso closed stronger versus the dollar on the back of rising international copper prices and institutional dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP467.20 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP467.80, while trading in a range of CLP466.80 to CLP469.00.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of the its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Monday at an average rate of CLP468.29. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.4 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower on institutional demand for fixed-income instruments.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.58%, down from 2.62% Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.88%, versus 2.90% in the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 09-05-11 2020GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110509e759001em\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (chile near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) \cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \